    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6620" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναισθ-ησία</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lack of sensation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				74e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				495
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετ᾽ ἀναισθησίας</span>”
				<i>without the aid of sense-perception,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					52b
				</span></i>
			; <i>unconsciousness, Ax.</i><i><span class="en">
				365d
			</span></i>; <i>insensibility</i> to pleasure or pain, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1109a4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1119a7
			</span></i>; <i>insensibility</i> under surgical treatment, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.140
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>mental obtuseness,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				22.64
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>stupor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				1.5
			</span></i>.</div>
